==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|filu||many}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*felu}}. More at {{term|fele}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/fiːl/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-viel.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|de|pronoun}}

# [[much]], [[a lot]]
#: {{usex|Es ist '''viel''' passiert.|t=Much has happened.|lang=de}}

====Usage notes====
* Compare the similar, but semantically different pronoun {{m|de|vieles}}.

===Adjective===
{{de-adj|mehr|meisten}}

# [[much]], [[many]]
#: {{usex|{{l/de|er|Er} {{l/de|haben|hat}} '''viel''' {{l/de|Geld}} {{l/de|verloren}}.|t=He lost much money.|lang=de}}

====Usage notes====
* The adjective is left unchanged in the singular if its not preceded by an article or determiner (see example sentence above). Otherwise it is declined like a normal adjective: ''viel'''e''' Kinder'', ''das viel'''e''' Geld''.
* The comparative form {{m|de|mehr}} is invariable and never declined. It cannot be preceded by any article or determiner.

===Adverb===
{{de-adv|mehr|meisten}}

# [[much]], [[a lot]]
#: {{usex|Wir haben '''viel''' gelacht.|t=We laughed a lot.|lang=de}}

===See also===
* {{l/de|manch}}

